{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses said, when YHWH gives you.</b> Moses said: what we prayed for — that YHWH would give you food in the evening, so that you may know that the blessed El brought you out — our desire is that He give you in the evening meat to eat, but not to glut yourselves in the manner of the Egyptians, who have nothing before them but their bodies; and that in the morning He give you bread only to satisfy you, so that it be sufficient to fill your need." "<b>When YHWH hears your complaints.</b> And what we prayed for — that you would see the glory of YHWH — our desire is that He give you these things in order that it be shown to you that your complaints are against Him, and that He has heard your complaints."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:49.045829061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}